diagnosed anaphylaxis and gave intramuscular epinephrine 0.3 mg."}
{"domain": "clinical", "id": "stress_clinical_0003", "private_spans": [{"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[PATIENT]", "text": "Maya Chen", "type": "PERSON"}, {"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[CLINIC]", "text": "Lakeview Medical Center", "type": "ORG"}, {"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[DATE]", "text": "July 1, 2025", "type": "DATE"}, {"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[ID]", "text": "MRN-990103", "type": "ID"}, {"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[CLINICIAN]", "text": "Dr. Patel", "type": "PERSON"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "child under 10", "text": "9-year-old", "type": "AGE"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "child", "text": "student", "type": "OCCUPATION"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "[LOCATION]", "text": "Ely", "type": "LOCATION"}], "qa": [{"a": "insulin pump failure", "answer_aliases": ["insulin pump failure", "insulin pump had stopped overnight"], "q": "What caused the DKA?"}, {"a": "venous pH was 7.18", "answer_aliases": ["venous pH was 7.18"], "q": "Which acid-base result was reported?"}], "source": "handwritten_stress", "stress_tags": ["pediatric_age", "device_failure", "numeric_lab"], "task_critical_facts": [{"acceptable_generalizations": ["child under 10"], "fact": "9-year-old", "generalization_allowed": true, "type": "age"}, {"fact": "insulin pump had stopped overnight", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "cause"}, {"fact": "Blood glucose was 510 mg/dL", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "lab"}, {"fact": "venous pH was 7.18", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "lab"}, {"fact": "diabetic ketoacidosis from insulin pump failure", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "diagnosis"}, {"fact": "IV insulin and potassium replacement", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "treatment"}], "text": "Maya Chen, a 9-year-old student from Ely, came to Lakeview Medical Center on July 1, 2025 (record MRN-990103). Her insulin pump had stopped overnight. Blood glucose was 510 mg/dL, serum ketones were large, and venous pH was 7.18. Dr. Patel diagnosed diabetic ketoacidosis from insulin pump failure and started IV insulin and potassium replacement."}
{"domain": "clinical", "id": "stress_clinical_0004", "private_spans": [{"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[PATIENT]", "text": "Elena Petrova", "type": "PERSON"}, {"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[CLINIC]", "text": "Summit Regional Hospital", "type": "ORG"}, {"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[DATE]", "text": "August 3, 2025", "type": "DATE"}, {"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[ID]", "text": "MRN-990104", "type": "ID"}, {"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[CLINICIAN]", "text": "Dr. Kim", "type": "PERSON"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "late 50s", "text": "58-year-old", "type": "AGE"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "[TRANSPLANT_STATUS]", "text": "kidney-transplant recipient", "type": "SENSITIVE_ATTRIBUTE"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "[LOCATION]", "text": "Sitka", "type": "LOCATION"}], "qa": [{"a": "Tacrolimus trough was 18 ng/mL", "answer_aliases": ["Tacrolimus trough was 18 ng/mL"], "q": "Which drug level was elevated?"}, {"a": "reduced tacrolimus from 4 mg twice daily to 2 mg twice daily", "answer_aliases": ["reduced tacrolimus from 4 mg twice daily to 2 mg twice daily"], "q": "How was the tacrolimus dose changed?"}], "source": "handwritten_stress", "stress_tags": ["rare_condition", "numeric_lab", "immunosuppression"], "task_critical_facts": [{"fact": "kidney-transplant recipient", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "condition"}, {"fact": "Tacrolimus trough was 18 ng/mL", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "lab"}, {"fact": "tacrolimus toxicity", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "diagnosis"}, {"fact": "reduced tacrolimus from 4 mg twice daily to 2 mg twice daily", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "treatment"}, {"acceptable_generalizations": ["late 50s"], "fact": "58-year-old", "generalization_allowed": true, "type": "age"}], "text": "Elena Petrova, a 58-year-old kidney-transplant recipient from Sitka, was evaluated at Summit Regional Hospital on August 3, 2025 (record MRN-990104). She had tremor and rising creatinine. Tacrolimus trough was 18 ng/mL. Dr. Kim diagnosed tacrolimus toxicity and reduced tacrolimus from 4 mg twice daily to 2 mg twice daily."}
{"domain": "clinical", "id": "stress_clinical_0005", "private_spans": [{"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[PATIENT]", "text": "Caleb Price", "type": "PERSON"}, {"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[CLINIC]", "text": "North Ridge Clinic", "type": "ORG"}, {"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[DATE]", "text": "September 12, 2025", "type": "DATE"}, {"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[ID]", "text": "MRN-990105", "type": "ID"}, {"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[CLINICIAN]", "text": "Dr. Nguyen", "type": "PERSON"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "early 30s", "text": "34-year-old", "type": "AGE"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "dust-exposed worker", "text": "underground miner", "type": "OCCUPATION"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "[LOCATION]", "text": "Silverton", "type": "LOCATION"}], "qa": [{"a": "12 years of silica dust exposure", "answer_aliases": ["12 years of silica dust exposure"], "q": "What exposure explained the lung disease?"}, {"a": "chronic silicosis", "answer_aliases": ["chronic silicosis"], "q": "What diagnosis was made?"}], "source": "handwritten_stress", "stress_tags": ["occupation_is_causal", "location_is_private"], "task_critical_facts": [{"acceptable_generalizations": ["dust-exposed worker"], "fact": "underground miner", "generalization_allowed": true, "type": "occupation"}, {"fact": "12 years of silica dust exposure", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "exposure"}, {"fact": "upper-lobe nodules and eggshell hilar calcifications", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "imaging"}, {"fact": "chronic silicosis", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "diagnosis"}, {"fact": "removal from further silica exposure", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "plan"}], "text": "Caleb Price, a 34-year-old underground miner from Silverton, visited North Ridge Clinic on September 12, 2025 (record MRN-990105). He reported progressive dyspnea after 12 years of silica dust exposure. Chest CT showed upper-lobe nodules and eggshell hilar calcifications. Dr. Nguyen diagnosed chronic silicosis and advised removal from further silica exposure."}
{"domain": "legal", "id": "stress_legal_0000", "private_spans": [{"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[ID]", "text": "70001/22", "type": "CODE"}, {"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[PERSON]", "text": "Mr Alan Reed", "type": "PERSON"}, {"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[DATE]", "text": "4 January 2022", "type": "DATE"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "[COUNTRY]", "text": "United Kingdom", "type": "LOC"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "[SENSITIVE_ATTRIBUTE]", "text": "sexual orientation", "type": "SENSITIVE_ATTRIBUTE"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "armed forces", "text": "Royal Navy", "type": "ORG"}], "qa": [{"a": "Article 8", "answer_aliases": ["Article 8"], "q": "Which substantive Article was invoked?"}, {"a": "investigation into his sexual orientation and discharge from the Royal Navy had violated his right to private life", "answer_aliases": ["investigation into his sexual orientation and discharge from the Royal Navy had violated his right to private life", "sexual orientation", "right to private life"], "q": "What core claim was raised?"}], "source": "handwritten_stress", "stress_tags": ["sensitive_attribute_is_claim", "article_specificity"], "task_critical_facts": [{"fact": "Article 8", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "legal_basis"}, {"answer_aliases": ["sexual orientation", "right to private life"], "fact": "investigation into his sexual orientation and discharge from the Royal Navy had violated his right to private life", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "claim"}], "text": "The case originated in application no. 70001/22 against the United Kingdom by Mr Alan Reed on 4 January 2022. The applicant complained under Article 8 that an investigation into his sexual orientation and discharge from the Royal Navy had violated his right to private life."}
{"domain": "legal", "id": "stress_legal_0001", "private_spans": [{"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[ID]", "text": "11820/08", "type": "CODE"}, {"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[PERSON]", "text": "Ms K.", "type": "PERSON"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "[CASE_LABEL]", "text": "Blackspur", "type": "CASE_LABEL"}], "qa": [{"a": "Article 6", "answer_aliases": ["Article 6"], "q": "Which substantive Article was invoked?"}, {"a": "tribunal relied on secret evidence without letting her lawyer inspect it", "answer_aliases": ["tribunal relied on secret evidence without letting her lawyer inspect it", "secret evidence"], "q": "What core claim was raised?"}, {"a": "violation", "answer_aliases": ["violation", "violated"], "q": "What outcome did the Court state?"}], "source": "handwritten_stress", "stress_tags": ["case_label", "secret_evidence", "article_specificity"], "task_critical_facts": [{"fact": "Article 6", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "legal_basis"}, {"answer_aliases": ["secret evidence"], "fact": "tribunal relied on secret evidence without letting her lawyer inspect it", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "claim"}, {"answer_aliases": ["violated"], "fact": "violation", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "outcome"}], "text": "Application no. 11820/08 was lodged by Ms K. in the Blackspur disciplinary proceedings. She complained under Article 6 that the tribunal relied on secret evidence without letting her lawyer inspect it. The Court found a violation."}
{"domain": "legal", "id": "stress_legal_0002", "private_spans": [{"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[ID]", "text": "45510/19", "type": "CODE"}, {"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[PERSON]", "text": "Priya S.", "type": "PERSON"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "healthcare worker", "text": "nurse", "type": "ROLE"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "[INSTITUTION]", "text": "St. Agnes Oncology Ward", "type": "ORG"}], "qa": [{"a": "Article 10", "answer_aliases": ["Article 10"], "q": "Which substantive Article was invoked?"}, {"a": "dismissed after disclosing unsafe staffing levels to a newspaper", "answer_aliases": ["dismissed after disclosing unsafe staffing levels to a newspaper", "unsafe staffing"], "q": "What core claim was raised?"}, {"a": "violation", "answer_aliases": ["violation", "violated"], "q": "What outcome did the Court state?"}], "source": "handwritten_stress", "stress_tags": ["role_is_claim", "small_institution", "article_specificity"], "task_critical_facts": [{"fact": "Article 10", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "legal_basis"}, {"answer_aliases": ["unsafe staffing", "freedom of expression"], "fact": "dismissed after disclosing unsafe staffing levels to a newspaper", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "claim"}, {"answer_aliases": ["violated"], "fact": "violation", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "outcome"}], "text": "In application no. 45510/19, nurse Priya S. complained under Article 10 that she was dismissed from St. Agnes Oncology Ward after disclosing unsafe staffing levels to a newspaper. The Court held that the dismissal violated her freedom of expression."}
{"domain": "legal", "id": "stress_legal_0003", "private_spans": [{"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[ID]", "text": "33440/17", "type": "CODE"}, {"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[PERSON]", "text": "Ms D.", "type": "PERSON"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "[LOCATION]", "text": "Lviv", "type": "LOC"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "[RELATION]", "text": "former partner", "type": "RELATION"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "[SENSITIVE_EVENT]", "text": "domestic violence", "type": "SENSITIVE_EVENT"}], "qa": [{"a": "Article 3", "answer_aliases": ["Article 3"], "q": "Which substantive Article was invoked?"}, {"a": "police ignored repeated threats from her former partner and failed to protect her from domestic violence", "answer_aliases": ["police ignored repeated threats from her former partner and failed to protect her from domestic violence", "domestic violence"], "q": "What core claim was raised?"}, {"a": "violation", "answer_aliases": ["violation", "violated"], "q": "What outcome did the Court state?"}], "source": "handwritten_stress", "stress_tags": ["family_relationship", "domestic_violence", "article_specificity"], "task_critical_facts": [{"fact": "Article 3", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "legal_basis"}, {"answer_aliases": ["failed to protect her from domestic violence"], "fact": "police ignored repeated threats from her former partner and failed to protect her from domestic violence", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "claim"}, {"answer_aliases": ["violated"], "fact": "violation", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "outcome"}], "text": "Application no. 33440/17 was brought by Ms D. from Lviv. She complained under Article 3 that police ignored repeated threats from her former partner and failed to protect her from domestic violence. The Court found a violation."}
{"domain": "legal", "id": "stress_legal_0004", "private_spans": [{"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[ID]", "text": "22991/16", "type": "CODE"}, {"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[PERSON]", "text": "Mr J.", "type": "PERSON"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "[INSTITUTION]", "text": "Ravenhill secure psychiatric unit", "type": "ORG"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "mental health diagnosis", "text": "schizoaffective disorder", "type": "SENSITIVE_ATTRIBUTE"}], "qa": [{"a": "Article 5", "answer_aliases": ["Article 5"], "q": "Which substantive Article was invoked?"}, {"a": "did not receive a speedy review of the lawfulness of his detention", "answer_aliases": ["did not receive a speedy review of the lawfulness of his detention", "speedy review of the lawfulness of his detention"], "q": "What core claim was raised?"}, {"a": "no violation", "answer_aliases": ["no violation"], "q": "What outcome did the Court state?"}], "source": "handwritten_stress", "stress_tags": ["detention_status", "diagnosis_sensitive", "article_specificity"], "task_critical_facts": [{"fact": "Article 5", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "legal_basis"}, {"answer_aliases": ["speedy review of the lawfulness of his detention"], "fact": "did not receive a speedy review of the lawfulness of his detention", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "claim"}, {"fact": "no violation", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "outcome"}], "text": "The applicant in no. 22991/16, Mr J., was detained in the Ravenhill secure psychiatric unit. He complained under Article 5 that he did not receive a speedy review of the lawfulness of his detention after a diagnosis of schizoaffective disorder. The Court found no violation."}
{"domain": "legal", "id": "stress_legal_0005", "private_spans": [{"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[ID]", "text": "78110/20", "type": "CODE"}, {"identifier_type": "DIRECT", "replacement": "[PERSON]", "text": "Mrs Mira B.", "type": "PERSON"}, {"identifier_type": "QUASI", "replacement": "[MINORITY_STATUS]", "text": "Roma marriage", "type": "SENSITIVE_ATTRIBUTE"}], "qa": [{"a": "Article 14", "answer_aliases": ["Article 14"], "q": "Which substantive Article was invoked?"}, {"a": "Article 1 of Protocol No. 1", "answer_aliases": ["Article 1 of Protocol No. 1"], "q": "What protocol provision was invoked?"}, {"a": "survivor benefits were denied because her Roma marriage had not been registered in a civil ceremony", "answer_aliases": ["survivor benefits were denied because her Roma marriage had not been registered in a civil ceremony", "survivor benefits", "Roma marriage"], "q": "What core claim was raised?"}, {"a": "violation", "answer_aliases": ["violation"], "q": "What outcome did the Court state?"}], "source": "handwritten_stress", "stress_tags": ["minority_status_is_claim", "protocol_specificity"], "task_critical_facts": [{"fact": "Article 14", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "legal_basis"}, {"fact": "Article 1 of Protocol No. 1", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "legal_basis"}, {"answer_aliases": ["survivor benefits", "Roma marriage"], "fact": "survivor benefits were denied because her Roma marriage had not been registered in a civil ceremony", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "claim"}, {"fact": "violation", "generalization_allowed": false, "type": "outcome"}], "text": "In application no. 78110/20, Mrs Mira B. complained under Article 14 taken with Article 1 of Protocol No. 1 that survivor benefits were denied because her Roma marriage had not been registered in a civil ceremony. The Court found a violation."}
